    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326-a1-a47">

                <pb facs="0528" n="488" xml:id="pg488"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 47.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Private Secretary’s
                            Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">
                                February</hi> 20, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am directed by his excellency the
                    governor to acknowledge your letter of the 15th, and to inform you that his
                    excellency is advised that it furnishes no ground for an alteration of the views
                    respecting the presumed character of the ship Shenandoah, which have been
                    already communicated to you.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. L. WARDE, <hi rendition="#italic">Private
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Blanchard,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
